-- Meters, seconds, radians, Y up. Water level is `y = 0`.
-- Geographic origin = Union Square, `LAT0 = 37.7880, LON0 = -122.4075`.
-  `x = (lon - LON0) * 111320 * cos(LAT0 * PI/180)` (east is +x)
-  `z = -(lat - LAT0) * 110540` (north is -z, south is +z)
+- Meters, seconds, radians, Y up. Sea water level is `y = 0`.
+- Heights: `y = NAVD88 (GEOID18) height - 0.969 m` (mean sea level at NOAA station 9414290,
+  epoch 1983-2001). The world manifest records it as `datum.y0_navd88`.
+- Geographic origin = Union Square, `LAT0 = 37.7880, LON0 = -122.4075`. Positions are a local
+  transverse Mercator on NAD83(2011) centred there
+  (`+proj=tmerc +lat_0=37.7880 +lon_0=-122.4075 +k_0=1 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +ellps=GRS80 +units=m`):
+  x = easting (east is +x), z = -northing (north is -z, south is +z). Only the bake tools project;
+  if runtime code ever needs lat/lon, use `world.project(lat, lon, out)` / `world.unproject(x, z, out)`.
 - **Heading** `h` is a rotation about +Y. A car with heading `h` faces world direction
   `forward = (sin h, 0, cos h)`. So `object.rotation.y = h` points a model's local +Z
   along forward. Heading 0 faces south (+z); heading PI faces north.
