+**Streaming.** The world loads in 512 m tiles as the camera moves. All World queries stay
+synchronous and allocation-free, and never throw or return NaN inside `bounds`. Within 1 km of the
+camera and along every shipped track corridor (pinned when `loadWorld` resolves) they are full
+detail. Elsewhere heights are coarse (8-16 m) and `collideCircle` uses simplified footprints, but
+bridges, viaducts and tunnels are always exact. `isLoaded(x, z)` says which.
+
 Required tracks (use real street routing via the OSM road graph): Embarcadero Sprint
 (Fisherman's Wharf -> Embarcadero -> Ferry Building -> Oracle Park), Lombard Zigzag
 (Russian Hill circuit incl. the crooked block of Lombard St and Hyde St), Golden Gate Run
